{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: the R6 corrected versioned publication at exact head b8c88c8fae77e094042fed6795957e3427efeb80, tree c9d468581c881f88b5ae2b6ed28de0b79660618c, on builder/security-r6-corrected-cohort-20261025 (review request 0e7fd9f4, promise ae5792b5). This review binds implementation request 3837ccc9 (promise b27cd0ab) to this one candidate. The head closes finding 2.2 of 6dd06d03 only. R7, finding 3.4, the planner's versioning and rollout question 587d629a and every hosted rollout remain open; landing deploys nothing and decides no rollout. It may land. The deploy notes at the end are material: a Worker that keeps serving the register 17 cohort needs a setting in the same deploy.\n\nRead order: I read the primary, notes/implementation/2026-10-25-security-r6-versioned-publication.md (artifact 57274cd0), first and in full, then the earlier note 2026-10-24-security-r6-creation-versions.md, the whole production diff (packages/scope, platform, cli, derive, git, replay, mcp, checkers, apps/room/page/src, scripts), the three documents, the new creation-versions witness file in full, the fixture repair, and the added, changed and removed test titles across the 44 test files. The 87 artifact events name exactly the 87 paths changed against the merge-base. The worktree /private/tmp/artroom-builder-security-r6-corrected-cohort-20261025 is clean at the head on its branch. The merge-base with Main is e645e9d2 (the documentation landing); the head is 30 commits above it. Main has since gained the sprint report 7b3dbd00; a merge of this head into 7b3dbd00 is conflict-free (merge-tree a2c2e5fd). The delta is 87 files, 1,456 insertions and 273 deletions.\n\nValidation record, as the request asked it to be assessed, with nothing relabeled:\n- Ordinary gate 68317 ran at be471af8 (tree 4979baae) and FAILED. Its seven pre-test stages passed, including the 40 compiler contexts; Vitest reported 3,578 passed, 1 failed and 3 skipped of 3,582 cases across 500 files with 0 unhandled errors; Node and Counting were not reached. The one red is packages/scope/test/demo-register.test.ts:34, \"an outside founder needs open policy and its actual child is indexed at genesis through enforced lineage\": the fixture set DEPLOYMENT without PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS, so the head's new default policy (newest cohort only) refused its register 17 install. That is the head's intended behavior, and the fixture lacked the allowance the head's own documentation requires. I verified the independent audit manifest (4 of 4 files by sha256, 809 bytes with the stated digest), its duplicate-ready addendum, and the raw result.json and stdout.log directly: expectedHead be471af8, expectedTree 4979baae, unchangedCheckpoint true, gatePassed false, stages whitespace through typecheck exit 0, test exit 1, \"Tests 1 failed | 3578 passed | 3 skipped (3582)\".\n- The repair commit b8c88c8f changes two files: one added line in that test (PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS listing register 17, directory 16 and destination 12) and one paragraph of the note. Production, configuration, dependencies and every other test are byte-identical to be471af8 (git diff be471af8 b8c88c8f). No module imports demo-register.test.ts; the only references outside it are comments and a path list.\n- Continuation 63650 ran at b8c88c8f (tree c9d46858) and passed: the Scope test compiler context exit 0, the whole demo-register file 2 of 2, the eleven-file Node list 42 of 42, Counting 55 of 55, no skips or unhandled errors, ten equal boundary snapshots, outer 42.8 seconds. I verified its audit manifest (3 of 3 files, 639 bytes with the stated digest) and its production-unchanged proof against be471af8.\n\nRuling on the gate. docs/testing.md says to run the gate once at the head you will send, and it allows a targeted rerun only when a gate fails in a test that reads a document and the repair changes only that document. This repair changed the failing test's own file, not a document it reads, so the letter of the carve-out does not name this case. I accept the continuation in place of a second ordinary gate, for these reasons: the only change is inside the one failing test file, which nothing else imports, and Vitest isolates test files, so the other 498 passed files and the 40 compiler contexts could not observe it; the rerun is exactly the carve-out's remedy (that file plus every step the gate never reached); and AGENTS.md forbids repeating whole suites, so a 23-minute repeat would have proven nothing about production. The ordinary gate at b8c88c8f is not claimed passed. The record is: gate 68317 FAILED at be471af8 on one fixture; continuation 63650 PASSED at b8c88c8f; production unchanged between them. Had the repair touched production, a shared test helper, or more than the failing file, I would have required a new ordinary gate, as in a4cdaecc.\n\nConditions of 3837ccc9, each checked in source:\n1. Cohort register 18, directory 17, membership 8, rules 10, destination 13, inbox 1: ARCHIVE_DEVICE_PUBLICATION_COHORT in packages/platform/src/archive-binding-wire.ts; NEWEST in platform/src/index.ts; DIRECTORY_OF maps register@18 to directory@17; SIBLINGS_OF adds directory@17; VERSION_DATA adds the three rows, reusing archiveRegister, archiveDeviceDirectory and destination4 data and rules with archiveDevicePublicationOrigin (directory 17, rules 10, destination 13, membership 8, device command). native-declarations.generated.ts adds three rows and removes none; versions.test.ts adds three golden rows and leaves the 62 old rows unchanged; its NEWEST assertion is now the explicit cohort.\n2. Historical evaluators preserved: destination@12 is not added to any dispatch list; every list gains only @13. judgeTimed admits native timed opens for @3 and @13 and records the admitted owner; pins 4 through 12 behave as before. archiveDeviceApplicationPublicationOrigin is unchanged. ARCHIVE_NATIVE_DATA adds directory@17 and destination@13 rows with their predecessors' digests and says equal bytes do not establish equivalence.\n3. Strict creation policy (finding 2.2): packages/scope/src/creation-versions.ts parses PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS (undefined selects the newest cohort; at most 8,192 bytes; at most 128 distinct pins that the catalog knows; null, malformed, duplicate, unknown or oversize input gives a null policy, which closes new platform genesis). permitsNewPlatformScope is applied at every creation path: api() create in worker.ts (an excluded pin needs a fixed-index hit, which permits lookup only), the indexed adapter in scope-index.ts (the policy is captured before any await and is part of the cache identity), admitChildCreation in creation-lineage.ts (an excluded child pin must already be known), and ScopeObject create and deliver in object.ts, where #permitsPlatformGenesis admits an excluded pin only for an exact existing applied genesis: active scope, bounded hash-checked birth, same address, kind, incarnation, pin and seed, null predecessor and current support. DeployedScope injects the policy even without DEPLOYMENT; ALLOW_OPEN_CREATION does not bypass it. Witnesses: the five cases of creation-versions.test.ts (the parser with ten invalid forms and the frozen result; cache identity without retaining the caller's environment; child refusal before the local and open-creation shortcuts; a real deployed object refusing the legacy and register 17 pins for new genesis and refusing the newest under a null policy; a legacy repeat accepted only with its sealed birth intact, refused after the body is altered, with reads and acts keeping the pin). The parent's witness, \"an old version is refused for a new scope and accepted for a live scope that pins it\", is met.\n4. Explicit public register 17 settings: installSelection keeps --register-policy open at register 17; the demo-register fixture and the two Page Start fixtures carry PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS for 17, 16 and 12; docs/deploy.md states that a Worker serving the public offer needs that allowance.\n5. Publication journey for the new cohort: destination@13 is added to the CLI protocol sets (new packages/cli/src/destination-protocol.ts, used by edit, propose and verify-cleanup), delivery.ts publish-file and publication policy, destination-host accepts, recovery and snapshot reads, site/publication.ts, reads.ts expiry projection, destination.ts cleanup and reservation paths, checkers job.ts reservation owners, Page edit and review lists, MCP #applicationRoom, archive target, host item and anchors, replay private names (register 18), invitations directory map and announcements. The witnesses are the added and parameterized cases listed by title in the test diff; the D1 destination-host case is parameterized over destination 5 and destination 13 with its original row kept, and the versions test's \"highest version\" oracle is replaced by the explicit cohort. No acceptance case is removed.\n6. Partial scope and open items: the note and the request say 2.2 only, R7 and 3.4 separate, the planner question 587d629a open, no rollout approval inferred, no deployment by the builder. True at this head.\n7. CLI: dap scope-index versions --manifest FILE rereads listed genesis identities and reports observedPins and usableCreationCohorts without emitting a setting; --cohort file-publication is the explicit historical selector (register 3) with a local selected marker excluded from the signed and attempted identity; the unqualified dap install default is now register@18 through NEWEST.\n8. Settings inventory: the PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS row names its three readers; the checker recognizes Object.hasOwn(env, \"LITERAL\") under a filewide guard that Object is the untouched global, with 18 negative specimens; the entry-point tripwire seals are updated for the twelve changed owners and the new parser file. The Node run of 42 passed at this head.\n\nDocument checks at b8c88c8f: git diff --check from e645e9d2 clean; check-commit-messages from e645e9d2 reports 30 checked, 0 flagged; section citations on an export exit 0 (4 known unresolved, unchanged); relative links and anchors in the five changed Markdown files, 63 checked, 0 broken; docs/deploy.md gains the Creation versions section the other pages link to.\n\nArchitecture: new versions instead of a patch to destination 12 keep every recorded derivation stable, which is the right choice for a replayed journal. The policy is one parser and one predicate applied at every creation path, with the native sealed birth as the only exception authority, and the cohort constant is the single source for defaults, CLI, Page and MCP. The cost is three catalog versions whose declaration bytes equal their predecessors; the code says so wherever it matters.\n\nSecurity: finding 2.2 is closed at all creation paths, including the object's own create and deliver; an invalid setting fails closed; neither ALLOW_OPEN_CREATION nor a missing DEPLOYMENT skips the policy in deployed objects; an index hit grants lookup, not creation; the setting grants no member, credential or host authority; the CLI selection marker is local; /health does not attest the policy and the documents say so. No new route, caller, secret or provider call.\n\nSimplification, nonblocking:\n- docs/testing.md should say that a repair confined to the failing test's own file is treated like a document repair (rerun that file and the unreached steps). This review had to decide that by reasoning; the rule should decide it next time.\n- The destination pin lists are repeated inline at about fifteen sites in destination.ts, destination-host.ts, delivery.ts, reads.ts, site/publication.ts and checkers/job.ts. The CLI now has a shared destination-protocol.ts; the same on the platform side would make the next version a one-line change.\n- apps/room/page/src/data.ts now admits rules@10 rooms in reviewPolicyOf and roomInitialization. That also enables existing register 17 rooms in the Page, consistent with the rules 10 policy item; worth knowing when the Page is next reviewed.\n\nDeploy notes for the planner:\n- Deploying this head makes new platform genesis newest-cohort-only on every Worker. A Worker that must keep creating under register 17, directory 16 and destination 12 (the fixed public offer, --register-policy open, dap-grow's existing register and any new room founded in an existing register 17 register) needs PLATFORM_CREATION_PINS set to [\"platform:register@17\",\"platform:directory@16\",\"platform:destination@12\"] in the same deploy. Without it, founding a new room in an existing register and the public offer refuse with unsupported-definition or not-found. The gate's one red demonstrated exactly that refusal. Existing scopes' reads, acts, archive and replay are unaffected.\n- The setting is per Worker. /health does not validate it; verify with a creation probe after rollout. deploy:scope --keep-vars preserves an existing value and does not populate one.\n- dap install now creates register@18 by default. R1 admits one configured register root, so a new-cohort register on an existing Worker needs an explicit root cutover or a separate Worker; docs/deploy.md Creation versions, steps 1 to 5, is the procedure. dap scope-index versions lists observed pins per saved manifest before choosing allowances.\n- Planner question 587d629a (version assignment and rollout) remains the planner's. This approval accepts the head's code and record; it is not a rollout decision.\n\nFindings: none blocking.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:57274cd079c8563e209e6e680c667dd1ab6ce3cb","binding":"assigned","head":"b8c88c8fae77e094042fed6795957e3427efeb80","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ae5792b50654850297e37ae1c38309c54b9deaa1\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b27cd0ab48049b8a773174d6fba0516725bfb62d\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#gi